From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-BUILD-001 the names people read say Darni: chrome://version and the blocker's name

ReArc was renamed Darni (the bridge release, RELEASES.md "ReArc is now Darni").
Only what a person reads changes. Two strings in the engine are read by people:

1. chrome/browser/ui/webui/version/version_ui.cc: the version line of
   chrome://version, which the app menu's "About Chromium Engine" opens, said
   "ReArc 156.0.8078.109" (app/002). It says "Darni 156.0.8078.109".
2. chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_content_blocker.cc: the built-in blocker's
   manifest name and description, "ReArc Blocker" and "ReArc's built-in ad and
   tracker blocking." (tab/095). The name is the "Extension:" row of the task
   manager. They say "Darni Blocker" and "Darni's built-in ad and tracker
   blocking.".

What does not change, on purpose:
- PRODUCT_SHORTNAME=ReArc in BRANDING (chrome/002). The Safe Storage Keychain
  item "ReArc Safe Storage" / "ReArc" is named from it, and existing profiles
  are encrypted with that item's key. shell/scripts/release/
  check-safe-storage-name.py fails a release whose engine names another item.
- MAC_BUNDLE_ID=com.rearc.browser and the helper and framework ids under it.
- The blocker's extension IDs and manifest keys (kManifestKeys), so Chromium's
  stored state for it (the indexed rulesets, keyed by extension ID) is the
  same extension's. A name is not part of an extension's identity.
- The "ReArc Blocker" folder in the user data directory, which holds the
  prepared bundles of installed copies.
- Log lines ("ReArc bridge:", "ReArc Blocker:"), the "[ReArc Boost]" console
  prefix, the ReArc* C ABI names and every rearc_ file and feature name.
- The placeholder main menu's title in rearc_app_delegate_mac.mm: AppKit never
  shows a main menu's own title, and the host replaces the menu.

No ABI change: REARC_ABI_MINOR_VERSION and the bridge version stay as tab/097
(or tab/098, when it is in the series) leaves them. Applies after tab/095; it
touches no line another patch's hunk has in its context (checked against the
tree after tab/097 and after tab/098).

Not built: written from `git show` of the overlay tree, with no write to
engine/chromium/src or out/ (another build was running). Needs an engine
rebuild of two translation units to take effect.

Last rebased: 2026-11-19 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.109, after tab/097.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_content_blocker.cc | 7 +++++--
 chrome/browser/ui/webui/version/version_ui.cc        | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_content_blocker.cc b/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_content_blocker.cc
index 7922dd3..2e037a4 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_content_blocker.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_content_blocker.cc
@@ -543,8 +543,11 @@ std::optional<Bundle> PrepareBundle(const base::FilePath& source,
 base::DictValue BlockerManifest(const Bundle& bundle, int slot) {
   base::DictValue manifest;
   manifest.Set("manifest_version", 3);
-  manifest.Set("name", "ReArc Blocker");
-  manifest.Set("description", "ReArc's built-in ad and tracker blocking.");
+  // What people read (the task manager's "Extension:" row): ReArc was renamed
+  // Darni. The extension IDs, the manifest keys, the "ReArc Blocker" folder in
+  // the user data directory and the log prefix keep the old name.
+  manifest.Set("name", "Darni Blocker");
+  manifest.Set("description", "Darni's built-in ad and tracker blocking.");
   manifest.Set("version", ExtensionVersion(bundle.version));
   manifest.Set("key", kManifestKeys[slot]);
   manifest.Set("incognito", "split");
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/version/version_ui.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/version/version_ui.cc
index b87342a..efd7a88 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/version/version_ui.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/version/version_ui.cc
@@ -250,7 +250,7 @@ void VersionUI::AddVersionDetailStrings(content::WebUIDataSource* html_source) {
   // Data strings.
   html_source->AddString(
       version_ui::kVersion,
-      base::StrCat({"ReArc ", version_info::GetVersionNumber()}));
+      base::StrCat({"Darni ", version_info::GetVersionNumber()}));
   html_source->AddString(version_ui::kVersionSuffix,
                          GetVersionInformationalSuffix());
 
